Write a Java program that takes an XPath expression as input and returns a Use selector. Make sure to provide an explanation of the purpose and functionality of the Use selector. You can use the `org.openxml.sel.UseSelector` class from the Open XML Toolkit (OXT) library. For example:

```java
import org.openxml.sel.UseSelector;
import org.openxml.sel.XPathContext;
import org.openxml.sel.XPathFunction;
import org.openxml.sel.XPathFunctionFactory;
import org.openxml.sel.XPathResult;
import org.openxml.sel.XPathSelector;

// Create an instance of the UseSelector class, specifying the XPath expression as the input
// and the output format as the optional output format.
UseSelector useSelector = new UseSelector(
    "//p[contains(text(), 'Hello, World!')]", 
    XPathContext.HTML, 
    XPathFunction.EMPTY, 
    XPathResult.CONTEXT
);

// Get the Use selector's output
String output = useSelector.select(null);

// Print the output
System.out.println(output);
```

